From fe0f543ec961704c75fdbe4ed610a3bcb0c7992f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tommy <tommy@pham.cc>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:22:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 71/73] Graphics options: internal resolution steps, FXAA/SSAA,
 anisotropic, sharp 2D, window filter

- Internal resolution like T5DR: TEKKEN4_INTERNAL_RES=lowest|native|1080p|1440p|4k|auto (scale = step height /
  448, fractional scales are exact thanks to the sprite snapping); auto = the window monitor's step, at most 1080p
  on integrated graphics (GL renderer string). PS2X_GS_HW_SCALE=<number or step> stays the raw override.
- TEKKEN4_AA=off|fxaa (default)|ssaa<f>|msaa<n>|smaa, '+' combines: FXAA 3.11 quality on the presented picture;
  SSAA draws the targets at scale * f and averages down (msaa<n> = n samples per pixel as SSAA: real MSAA is not
  usable with the GS emulation's feedback reads); smaa falls back to FXAA.
- TEKKEN4_ANISO=1..16 (default 8): filtered taps along the footprint's long axis for filtered 3D draws (no mipmaps).
- CLAMP region modes are now filtered bilinear like the GS (were point sampled; PS2X_GL_REGION_LINEAR=0: old).
- TEKKEN4_HUD=sharp: sharp bilinear for magnified 2D sprites of game textures (soft = the GS's bilinear).
- Window: TEKKEN4_WINDOW_FILTER=area (default: area average when the picture is larger than the window, bilinear
  when smaller)|sharp|bilinear|nearest; the shared picture was drawn nearest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
